{"id":1754318,"retrievedAt":"2026-08-23T11:41:31.011Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":99,"name":"Documentary"},{"id":10751,"name":"Family"}],"homepage":"","id":1754318,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_title":"Vibrant Aviary","overview":"A short travelling documentary exploring Ibarbo Park, a family recreation and educational destination in Yogyakarta, Indonesia. Home to nearly a hundred varieties of birds, a mini zoo, animal-feeding experiences, and colorful fantasy-themed photo spots, the park offers a vibrant world where recreation and education come together.  Created by a group of 11th-grade Film Production students from BOPKRI 1 Vocational High School Yogyakarta, the documentary captures Ibarbo Park during a particular moment in its development—when its now-open Kota Kartun (Cartoon City) area was still being promoted as “coming soon.” Following Neta as the cheerful host as she guides the audience through the largest souvenir center and aviary in Yogyakarta.  Completed on November 1, 2024, this unreleased short documentary remains a snapshot of Ibarbo Park as it was during production, preserving a small piece of the attraction’s history before its continued transformation.","popularity":0.0286,"poster_path":null,"production_companies":[{"id":308327,"logo_path":null,"name":"One Life Production","origin_country":""}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"ID","name":"Indonesia"}],"release_date":"2024-11-01","revenue":0,"runtime":6,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[],"status":"Released","tagline":"Becoming Indonesia’s largest educational tourism destination","title":"Vibrant Aviary","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":6429162,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"Garneta Giovanni Elysia","original_name":"Garneta Giovanni Elysia","popularity":0,"profile_pa